{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"MutationCache"},{"type":"text","value":" is the storage for mutations."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Normally, you will not interact with the MutationCache directly and instead use the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"QueryClient"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { MutationCache } from 'react-query'\n\nconst mutationCache = new MutationCache({\n  onError: error => {\n    console.log(error)\n  },\n  onSuccess: data => {\n    console.log(data)\n  },\n})","lang":"js"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Its available methods are:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"#mutationcachegetall","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"getAll"}]}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"#mutationcachesubscribe","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"subscribe"}]}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"#mutationcacheclear","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"clear"}]}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Options"}]}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"onError?: (error: unknown, variables: unknown, context: unknown, mutation: Mutation) => void"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Optional"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"This function will be called if some mutation encounters an error."}]}]}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"onSuccess?: (data: unknown, variables: unknown, context: unknown, mutation: Mutation) => void"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Optional"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"This function will be called if some mutation is successful."}]}]}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"onMutate?: (variables: unknown, mutation: Mutation) => void"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Optional"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"This function will be called before some mutation executes."}]}]}]}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"global-callbacks","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Global callbacks"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"onError"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"onSuccess"},{"type":"text","value":" and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"onMutate"},{"type":"text","value":" callbacks on the MutationCache can be used to handle these events on a global level. They are different to "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"defaultOptions"},{"type":"text","value":" provided to the QueryClient because:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"defaultOptions"},{"type":"text","value":" can be overridden by each Mutation - the global callbacks will "},{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"always"}]},{"type":"text","value":" be called."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"onMutate"},{"type":"text","value":" does not allow returning a context value."}]}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"mutationcache-getall","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"mutationCache.getAll"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"getAll"},{"type":"text","value":" returns all mutations within the cache."}]},{"type":"blockquote","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Note: This is not typically needed for most applications, but can come in handy when needing more information about a mutation in rare scenarios"}]}]},{"type":"code","value":"const mutations = mutationCache.getAll()","lang":"js"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Returns"}]}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Mutation[]"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Mutation instances from the cache"}]}]}]}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"mutationcache-subscribe","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"mutationCache.subscribe"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"subscribe"},{"type":"text","value":" method can be used to subscribe to the mutation cache as a whole and be informed of safe/known updates to the cache like mutation states changing or mutations being updated, added or removed."}]},{"type":"code","value":"const callback = mutation => {\n  console.log(mutation)\n}\n\nconst unsubscribe = mutationCache.subscribe(callback)","lang":"js"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Options"}]}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"callback: (mutation?: Mutation) => void"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"This function will be called with the mutation cache any time it is updated."}]}]}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Returns"}]}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"unsubscribe: Function => void"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"This function will unsubscribe the callback from the mutation cache."}]}]}]}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"mutationcache-clear","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"mutationCache.clear"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"clear"},{"type":"text","value":" method can be used to clear the cache entirely and start fresh."}]},{"type":"code","value":"mutationCache.clear()","lang":"js"}],"headings":[{"id":"global-callbacks","text":"Global callbacks","level":2},{"id":"mutationcache-getall","text":"mutationCache.getAll","level":2},{"id":"mutationcache-subscribe","text":"mutationCache.subscribe","level":2},{"id":"mutationcache-clear","text":"mutationCache.clear","level":2}]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"\nThe `MutationCache` is the storage for mutations.\n\n**Normally, you will not interact with the MutationCache directly and instead use the `QueryClient`.**\n\n```js\nimport { MutationCache } from 'react-query'\n\nconst mutationCache = new MutationCache({\n  onError: error => {\n    console.log(error)\n  },\n  onSuccess: data => {\n    console.log(data)\n  },\n})\n```\n\nIts available methods are:\n\n- [`getAll`](#mutationcachegetall)\n- [`subscribe`](#mutationcachesubscribe)\n- [`clear`](#mutationcacheclear)\n\n**Options**\n\n- `onError?: (error: unknown, variables: unknown, context: unknown, mutation: Mutation) => void`\n  - Optional\n  - This function will be called if some mutation encounters an error.\n- `onSuccess?: (data: unknown, variables: unknown, context: unknown, mutation: Mutation) => void`\n  - Optional\n  - This function will be called if some mutation is successful.\n- `onMutate?: (variables: unknown, mutation: Mutation) => void`\n  - Optional\n  - This function will be called before some mutation executes.\n\n## Global callbacks\n\nThe `onError`, `onSuccess` and `onMutate` callbacks on the MutationCache can be used to handle these events on a global level. They are different to `defaultOptions` provided to the QueryClient because:\n\n- `defaultOptions` can be overridden by each Mutation - the global callbacks will **always** be called.\n- `onMutate` does not allow returning a context value.\n\n## `mutationCache.getAll`\n\n`getAll` returns all mutations within the cache.\n\n> Note: This is not typically needed for most applications, but can come in handy when needing more information about a mutation in rare scenarios\n\n```js\nconst mutations = mutationCache.getAll()\n```\n\n**Returns**\n\n- `Mutation[]`\n  - Mutation instances from the cache\n\n## `mutationCache.subscribe`\n\nThe `subscribe` method can be used to subscribe to the mutation cache as a whole and be informed of safe/known updates to the cache like mutation states changing or mutations being updated, added or removed.\n\n```js\nconst callback = mutation => {\n  console.log(mutation)\n}\n\nconst unsubscribe = mutationCache.subscribe(callback)\n```\n\n**Options**\n\n- `callback: (mutation?: Mutation) => void`\n  - This function will be called with the mutation cache any time it is updated.\n\n**Returns**\n\n- `unsubscribe: Function => void`\n  - This function will unsubscribe the callback from the mutation cache.\n\n## `mutationCache.clear`\n\nThe `clear` method can be used to clear the cache entirely and start fresh.\n\n```js\nmutationCache.clear()\n```\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\nid: MutationCache\ntitle: MutationCache\n---\n\nThe `MutationCache` is the storage for mutations.\n\n**Normally, you will not interact with the MutationCache directly and instead use the `QueryClient`.**\n\n```js\nimport { MutationCache } from 'react-query'\n\nconst mutationCache = new MutationCache({\n  onError: error => {\n    console.log(error)\n  },\n  onSuccess: data => {\n    console.log(data)\n  },\n})\n```\n\nIts available methods are:\n\n- [`getAll`](#mutationcachegetall)\n- [`subscribe`](#mutationcachesubscribe)\n- [`clear`](#mutationcacheclear)\n\n**Options**\n\n- `onError?: (error: unknown, variables: unknown, context: unknown, mutation: Mutation) => void`\n  - Optional\n  - This function will be called if some mutation encounters an error.\n- `onSuccess?: (data: unknown, variables: unknown, context: unknown, mutation: Mutation) => void`\n  - Optional\n  - This function will be called if some mutation is successful.\n- `onMutate?: (variables: unknown, mutation: Mutation) => void`\n  - Optional\n  - This function will be called before some mutation executes.\n\n## Global callbacks\n\nThe `onError`, `onSuccess` and `onMutate` callbacks on the MutationCache can be used to handle these events on a global level. They are different to `defaultOptions` provided to the QueryClient because:\n\n- `defaultOptions` can be overridden by each Mutation - the global callbacks will **always** be called.\n- `onMutate` does not allow returning a context value.\n\n## `mutationCache.getAll`\n\n`getAll` returns all mutations within the cache.\n\n> Note: This is not typically needed for most applications, but can come in handy when needing more information about a mutation in rare scenarios\n\n```js\nconst mutations = mutationCache.getAll()\n```\n\n**Returns**\n\n- `Mutation[]`\n  - Mutation instances from the cache\n\n## `mutationCache.subscribe`\n\nThe `subscribe` method can be used to subscribe to the mutation cache as a whole and be informed of safe/known updates to the cache like mutation states changing or mutations being updated, added or removed.\n\n```js\nconst callback = mutation => {\n  console.log(mutation)\n}\n\nconst unsubscribe = mutationCache.subscribe(callback)\n```\n\n**Options**\n\n- `callback: (mutation?: Mutation) => void`\n  - This function will be called with the mutation cache any time it is updated.\n\n**Returns**\n\n- `unsubscribe: Function => void`\n  - This function will unsubscribe the callback from the mutation cache.\n\n## `mutationCache.clear`\n\nThe `clear` method can be used to clear the cache entirely and start fresh.\n\n```js\nmutationCache.clear()\n```\n"}
